\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For any explicitly listed finite acyclic precedence graph on unit-length nonpreemptive jobs, can one deterministic polynomial-bit-time algorithm produce a minimum-makespan schedule on three identical machines and decide every binary deadline exactly?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For any explicitly listed finite acyclic precedence graph on unit-length nonpreemptive jobs, can one deterministic polynomial-bit-time algorithm produce a minimum-makespan schedule on three identical machines and decide every binary deadline exactly?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
